Subject: [PATCH 8/9] macos: apply the dialog window options to every dialog

Every dialog on macOS is meant to go through utility::setWindowOptions(),
which adds Qt::WindowStaysOnTopHint and makes the dialog window modal:

    void utility::setWindowOptions( QDialog * w )
    {
            if( utility::platformIsOSX() ){
                    w->setWindowFlags( w->windowFlags() | Qt::WindowStaysOnTopHint ) ;
                    w->setWindowModality( Qt::WindowModal ) ;
            }
    }

favorites2 never called it,so on macOS its window opens behind the main
window and never becomes the key window.  It can be dragged by its title
bar because that is the window server's doing,but no click reaches it,
its parent stays disabled by sirikali::disableAll() waiting for a
callback that can no longer fire,and the application has to be killed.
"sample" shows the process idle in mach_msg_trap throughout,so nothing
is stuck,the events simply have nowhere to go.

Reachable two ways: the Favorites button,and Create Volume for any
backend that is likeSsh().  keyDialog,which every other backend uses,
calls setWindowOptions() and is unaffected.

The function is a no op away from macOS.

The same omission is in every other dialog that is not keyDialog,plugin,
options,dialogmsg,dialogok or readonlywarning:

    Settings, Create Backend, Check For Updates, Help, File Manager,
    Config File Option and all seven per engine create option dialogs

None of them can be reached from the favorites window,which is why they
did not turn up in the same report,but they open the same way and would
sit behind the main window just as it did.  checkforupdateswindow.cpp
and engines/customcreateoptions.cpp did not include utility.h yet.

